  "body": "The repository's CREATOR-INTEL.md cites a local Telegram export and .gitignore explicitly excludes telegram_export.*, jrk_all_messages.txt, and related files. I audited all current branches, tags/releases, deletion history, repository objects, and the public fork network and could not find the underlying source corpus.\\n\\nCould you publish a privacy-preserving, redacted export containing only the puzzle creator's messages and the minimal replied-to message/context needed to interpret them? JSON with message IDs, timestamps, sender display name/ID (pseudonymized if necessary), reply_to_message_id, and text would be ideal. Media can be omitted except for creator-posted puzzle hints; personal information and unrelated participant messages should be removed.\\n\\nThis would let solvers verify exact wording and distinguish creator statements from later paraphrases without exposing the full private group history. A SHA-256 of the source export plus a description of the redaction process would also help establish provenance.",
